# MX-5 Mk4 Trophy

> A one make racing championship for the Mk4 (ND) Mazda MX-5, run with the
> BRSCC on UK circuits. Every car is built to a single sealed control
> specification on a Goodyear control tyre. The first season runs in 2027
> on the BRSCC MX-5 SuperCup grid; the Trophy takes its own slot on the
> BRSCC roster from 2028.

## Facts

- Championship: Mazda MX-5 Mk4 Trophy.
- Sanctioned by: BRSCC (British Racing and Sports Car Club), under MSUK.
- Car: Mazda MX-5 Mk4 (ND), one sealed control specification.
- Drivetrain: ZF sequential gearbox.
- Driver aids: ABS and traction control.
- Tyres: Goodyear hard compound control slick, plus a Goodyear wet.
- Tyre allocation: six sets of slicks per season.
- First season: 2027, sharing the BRSCC MX-5 SuperCup grid.
- From 2028: its own slot on the BRSCC roster.
- Not the same as the BRSCC MX-5 SuperCup, which is a Mk3 championship.
  In 2027 the two share a grid but are scored as separate championships.
- Licence required: ARDS test and an MSUK National licence.
- Championship partners: Goodyear (tyre partner), Thermal Road Repairs,
  AD Modular.

